§ `Section 76(2): the means of giving financial assistance`

-- (2): a reference to the giving of financial assistance "includes" a reference to the giving of financial assistance by means of the making of a loan,
-- the giving of a guarantee, the provision of security, the release of an obligation or the release of a debt "or otherwise".
-- src:7373 | (2) A reference in this section to the giving of financial assistance
-- src:7374 | includes a reference to the giving of financial assistance by means of
-- src:7375 | the making of a loan, the giving of a guarantee, the provision of
-- src:7376 | security, the release of an obligation or the release of a debt or
-- src:7377 | otherwise.
@ref s 76(2) (src:7373-7377)
GIVEN `the means` IS A `s 76(2) means of giving financial assistance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(2) the means is within the giving of financial assistance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the means`
    WHEN `s 76(2) the making of a loan` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 76(2) the giving of a guarantee` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 76(2) the provision of security` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 76(2) the release of an obligation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 76(2) the release of a debt` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to the giving of financial assistance by means of ... or otherwise" -- the list is not closed and the subsection says nothing of any other means

§ `Section 76(3) and (4): when the company is taken to have given the assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, an acquisition`

-- (3): taken to have given financial assistance for the purpose of an acquisition if (a) it gave the assistance for purposes that included the relevant purpose and
-- (b) the relevant purpose was a substantial purpose of the giving.
-- src:7379 | (3) For the purposes of this section, a company is taken to have
-- src:7380 | given financial assistance for the purpose of an acquisition or
-- src:7381 | proposed acquisition referred to in subsection (1) (called in this
-- src:7382 | subsection the relevant purpose) if —
-- src:7384 | (a) the company gave the financial assistance for purposes that
-- src:7385 | included the relevant purpose; and
-- src:7387 | (b) the relevant purpose was a substantial purpose of the
-- src:7388 | giving of the financial assistance.
@ref s 76(3) (src:7379-7388)
GIVEN `the company gave the financial assistance for purposes that included the purpose of the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the acquisition was a substantial purpose of the giving of the financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(3) the company is taken to have given the assistance for the purpose of the acquisition` MEANS
    IF    `the company gave the financial assistance for purposes that included the purpose of the acquisition`
      AND `the purpose of the acquisition was a substantial purpose of the giving of the financial assistance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "is taken to have given financial assistance for the purpose of an acquisition ... if" -- a deeming that adds to the ordinary meaning of "for the purpose of"; it does not say that other assistance was not given for that purpose (fork line F-A3)

-- (4): taken to have given financial assistance in connection with an acquisition if, when the assistance was given to a person, the company was aware that it
-- would financially assist (a) the acquisition by a person of shares or units of shares in the company; or (b) where shares in the company had already been acquired,
-- the payment by a person of any unpaid amount of the subscription payable for the shares, or of any calls on the shares.
-- src:7392 | (4) For the purposes of this section, a company is taken to have
-- src:7393 | given financial assistance in connection with an acquisition or
-- src:7398 | proposed acquisition referred to in subsection (1) if, when the
-- src:7399 | financial assistance was given to a person, the company was aware
-- src:7400 | that the financial assistance would financially assist —
-- src:7402 | (a) the acquisition by a person of shares or units of shares in
-- src:7403 | the company; or
-- src:7405 | (b) where shares in the company had already been acquired —
-- src:7406 | the payment by a person of any unpaid amount of the
-- src:7407 | subscription payable for the shares, or the payment of any
-- src:7408 | calls on the shares.
@ref s 76(4) (src:7392-7408)
GIVEN `when the assistance was given, the company was aware that it would financially assist the acquisition by a person of shares or units of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `when the assistance was given, the company was aware that it would financially assist the payment by a person of an unpaid amount of the subscription payable for shares already acquired, or of calls on them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(4) the company is taken to have given the assistance in connection with the acquisition` MEANS
    IF    `when the assistance was given, the company was aware that it would financially assist the acquisition by a person of shares or units of shares in the company`
       OR `when the assistance was given, the company was aware that it would financially assist the payment by a person of an unpaid amount of the subscription payable for shares already acquired, or of calls on them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "is taken to have given financial assistance in connection with an acquisition ... if, when the financial assistance was given to a person, the company was aware" -- a deeming that adds to the ordinary meaning of "in connection with" (fork line F-A3)

§ `Section 76(16): the ways of acquiring`

-- (16): a reference to an acquisition or proposed acquisition of shares or units of shares is a reference to any acquisition or proposed acquisition
-- "whether by way of purchase, subscription or otherwise".
-- src:8092 | (16) A reference in this section to an acquisition or proposed
-- src:8093 | acquisition of shares or units of shares is a reference to any
-- src:8094 | acquisition or proposed acquisition whether by way of purchase,
-- src:8095 | subscription or otherwise.
@ref s 76(16) (src:8092-8095)
GIVEN `the way of acquiring` IS A `s 76(16) way of acquiring`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(16) the way of acquiring is within the acquisition the section speaks of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way of acquiring`
    WHEN `s 76(16) purchase` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 76(16) subscription` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 76(16) some other way` THEN JUST TRUE   -- the text says "or otherwise": every way of acquiring is within the reference

§ `Section 76(17): contracts made before 15 May 1987`

-- (17): the section does not apply to the doing of any act or thing pursuant to a contract entered into before 15 May 1987, if the doing would have been lawful
-- had this Act not been enacted.
-- src:8097 | (17) This section does not apply in relation to the doing of any act or
-- src:8098 | thing pursuant to a contract entered into before 15 May 1987 if the
-- src:8099 | doing of that act or thing would have been lawful if this Act had not
-- src:8100 | been enacted.
@ref s 76(17) (src:8097-8100)
GIVEN `the date the contract was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the act or thing is done pursuant to that contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the doing of the act or thing would have been lawful if this Act had not been enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(17) the section does not apply to the act or thing` MEANS
    IF    `the act or thing is done pursuant to that contract`
      AND `the date the contract was entered into` LESS THAN Date 15 5 1987
      AND `the doing of the act or thing would have been lawful if this Act had not been enacted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply in relation to the doing of any act or thing pursuant to a contract entered into before 15 May 1987 if the doing of that act or thing would have been lawful if this Act had not been enacted" -- a failed "if" (marginal reading (a), fork line F-A4): JUST FALSE here means the exclusion does not take the act out of the section
